            <div xml:id="d767">

                <pb facs="0848" n="760" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg760"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.5151/174: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-07T14:00:00-05:00">October 7, 1933—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>75. Your 93, October 5, 4 p.m., and Consulate General’s October 5, 6 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">5</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="37" xml:id="d767-f1"/> In view of
                    possible conflicts of interests between the American groups known to be actively
                    interested in reaching an exchange agreement with Argentina, and between them
                    and holders of Argentine bonds, the Department is confident that you will
                    exercise care not to give the impression that this Government favors any
                    particular group or is in any way involved in the negotiations of these private
                    groups.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
